# Deny all web access to data/documents/unfiled/.
#
# INTENT CHANGE (Task 4.1 fix round 1). This file used to say
#   <Files *.djvu>
#   order allow,deny
#   allow from all
#   </Files>
# i.e. it was an exception INSIDE the denied data/ tree: unfiled .djvu uploads
# were fetchable by URL (measured at HEAD: 200, 60521 bytes on both servers).
# The server-configuration rule this project now ships denies the whole data/
# tree, so the exception was already overridden there - this file is brought into
# line with it rather than left saying the opposite, and it no longer carries the
# 2.2-only syntax that is a configuration error during URI mapping on an Apache
# 2.4 vhost without mod_access_compat (500, not the 403 this rule means).
#
# Why the denial is right: nothing in this tree builds a URL into this
# directory - the document viewer fetches pages through the relay
# (<relay>/org.freemedsoftware.module.<module>.GetDocumentPage), not from the
# filesystem path - and serving PHI from a guessable URL is the thing this
# change exists to stop. A site that needs the old behaviour should state an
# explicit, extension-restricted exception in its server configuration (see
# doc/DEPLOYMENT_HARDENING section 8), not here.
#
# Second layer only: nginx reads no .htaccess, and `AllowOverride None` ignores
# it. Both syntaxes are present and module-guarded.
<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
	Require all denied
</IfModule>
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
	order deny,allow
	deny from all
</IfModule>
